## Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 | **Language:** C# (.NET 10) | **Scope:** Integration tests (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test (Smell 3)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` line 87  
**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← hardcoded 3-second blocking wait
```

**Why it's a problem (even in integration tests):** A fixed 3 s sleep is non-deterministic — too short on slow CI, needlessly slow elsewhere. It makes the suite flaky and slower.

**Fix — use a polling wait with timeout:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures; wastes 3 s on every run even when the event fires in 50 ms.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic (Smell 1)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` lines 101–108  
**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Why it's a problem:** Only one branch ever executes — if the type is always `User`, the `PremiumUser` path is dead code giving false confidence. If it *is* a `PremiumUser`, the name assertion is never checked.

**Fix — write two explicit tests with deterministic setup:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;

    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden test gaps — one code path is never verified.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test / Unknown Test (Smell 4)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` lines 113–119  
**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion
}
```

**Why it's a problem:** This passes as long as no exception is thrown. Corrupt data, silently dropped inserts, or partial failures are all invisible.

**Fix — assert the observable effect:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count, "Not all bulk-inserted users were persisted.");
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — 100 % pass rate regardless of correctness.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette (Extended Catalog)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` lines 35–39  
**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
// ← 4 assertions, zero message parameters
```

**Why it's a problem:** When one assertion fails, the MSTest output says *"Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>"* with no contextual message — you must read the code to determine which property was wrong.

**Fix — add diagnostic messages:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name mismatch after round-trip.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email mismatch after round-trip.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive.");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage; developers must open the file to interpret failures.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✅

The remaining tests are well-structured:

| Method | Why it's good |
|--------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert; verifies the mutation |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behaviour verified with a clear null check |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count assertion is contextually obvious (3 inserts → 3 count) |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Async-safe, asserts end-state |

The `[TestInitialize]` fixture is tight — both fields are used by every test (no **General Fixture** smell). The in-memory SQLite connection is hermetic (no **Mystery Guest** smell despite the database usage).

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Method | Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` | Low (add 2 lines) | Eliminates false confidence |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` | Medium (split into 2 tests) | Closes dead-code gap |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` | Medium (add polling helper) | Reduces flakiness + saves 3 s |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` | Low (add message strings) | Faster failure triage |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests have catalogued smells. The three High-severity findings (#1–#3 above) represent real reliability risks. Fixing them is low-to-medium effort and will measurably improve suite trustworthiness.
